            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that both these structures have the same formula",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { C _ { 4 } H _ { 1 0 ^ { \\circ } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Such compounds with identical molecular formula but different structures are called structural isomers.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.372,
            0.722,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In addition to straight and branched carbon chains, some compounds have carbon atoms arranged in the form of a ring. For example, cyclohexane has the formula",
              "styles": [
